# Keep the build context small and free of secrets: the context is uploaded to Fly's remote
# builder. The build needs Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, rust-toolchain.toml, .cargo/, crates/ (with
# their assets and migrations), .sqlx/ and any data directories the crates include.
# `**/` patterns match at any depth; plain patterns only at the context root.

# Build output
**/target/
**/dist/

# Environment files and keys, at any depth. `.env.example` (placeholders only) is excluded too:
# the build never needs it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.p8
**/*.jks
# Same credential files as .gitignore: SSH keys, netrc, cloud credentials, direnv.
**/id_rsa*
**/id_dsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.netrc
**/credentials.json
**/.envrc

# VCS, CI and docs (root only: a crate may include its own README)
.git/
.github/
docs/
*.md

# Local tooling, editors and OS files
**/.remember/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.iml
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules/

# Container and host config
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
fly.toml
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yml
